    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1951-p17.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Choices A, C, and E rearrange to \\(y=kx,\\) and choice B rearranges to \\(xy=k.\\) But choice D gives \\(y=10-3x,\\) which is neither form.\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Direct proportion has the form \\(y=kx\\), while inverse proportion has the form \\(xy=k\\)",
